for doing this thing here on the mic

1039
00:43:33.325 --> 00:43:35.270
that was really, really awesome.

1040
00:43:35.270 --> 00:43:36.540
The first time that's really happened

1041
00:43:36.540 --> 00:43:41.020
I mean, it was disorienting at times, but in a good way.

1042
00:43:41.020 --> 00:43:43.980
And I appreciate the audience

1043
00:43:43.980 --> 00:43:46.630
and this position I'm in right now.

1044
00:43:46.630 --> 00:43:51.630
So the seat and it was, that is like for you too I mean,

1045
00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:56.273
that is like the exact plate, even,

1046
00:43:57.494 --> 00:43:58.327
what's cool about it

1047
00:43:58.327 --> 00:44:01.700
is even promoting what James had been doing from day one.

1048
00:44:01.700 --> 00:44:03.180
And so it's not surprising

1049
00:44:03.180 --> 00:44:04.770
that there was such an intersection there

1050
00:44:04.770 --> 00:44:08.020
because like, part of the reason Said Saeed was there

1051
00:44:08.020 --> 00:44:10.970
was because you told him about James Lawrence.

1052
00:44:10.970 --> 00:44:14.260
Cause I was doing podcasts with him a long time ago.

1053
00:44:14.260 --> 00:44:15.800
I've been talking about him forever.

1054
00:44:15.800 --> 00:44:20.310
I still feel like media is dropping the ball

1055
00:44:20.310 --> 00:44:23.350
in terms of giving this guy some love.

1056
00:44:23.350 --> 00:44:25.950
You know, I think this sort of eclipsed,

1057
00:44:25.950 --> 00:44:27.650
any kind of mainstream attention,

1058
00:44:27.650 --> 00:44:30.710
I'm delighted that the New York Times Green Light

1059
00:44:30.710 --> 00:44:32.540
you going out there and doing a story.

1060
00:44:32.540 --> 00:44:34.800
And I look forward to that story coming out.

1061
00:44:34.800 --> 00:44:36.080
But on the whole,

1062
00:44:36.080 --> 00:44:40.360
aside from a couple like sort of local news stories,

1063
00:44:40.360 --> 00:44:42.340
there hasn't been that much attention

1064
00:44:42.340 --> 00:44:44.550
as sports illustrated wrote an article on it.

1065
00:44:44.550 --> 00:44:47.010
I was really glad to see that they acknowledged

1066
00:44:47.010 --> 00:44:49.525
what he had done, but when we were on,

1067
00:44:49.525 --> 00:44:51.960
but they weren't all day when we were,

1068
00:44:51.960 --> 00:44:53.990
they weren't there, nobody else had showed up

1069
00:44:53.990 --> 00:44:58.990
except for you but on when we were there on the final day

1070
00:44:59.080 --> 00:45:02.623
and we're at the high school and on the football field,

1071
00:45:03.520 --> 00:45:06.170
I got wind that this Washington post article

1072
00:45:06.170 --> 00:45:08.230
had come out about James,

1073
00:45:08.230 --> 00:45:10.213
that I want to pull up right now.

1074
00:45:11.310 --> 00:45:13.100
Which we both kind of read together,

1075
00:45:13.100 --> 00:45:14.500
standing on the football field.

1076
00:45:14.500 --> 00:45:19.500
Well Sunny, who's James's wife comes up to me and says,

1077
00:45:22.720 --> 00:45:25.000
don't do what the Washington post did.

1078
00:45:25.000 --> 00:45:26.540
I'm like, wait, what?

1079
00:45:26.540 --> 00:45:27.690
Can we read this thing?

1080
00:45:27.690 --> 00:45:29.163
So we read this article,

1081
00:45:30.330 --> 00:45:32.330
it's titled Through Pain and Controversy,

1082
00:45:32.330 --> 00:45:36.370
the Iron Cowboy chase's 100 triathlons in 100 days.

1083
00:45:36.370 --> 00:45:40.873
The first, how does this open?

1084
00:45:45.924 --> 00:45:47.460
The second paragraph did they, oh yeah.

1085
00:45:47.460 --> 00:45:50.660
So when it's describing James,

1086
00:45:50.660 --> 00:45:53.660
the paragraph introducing and basically says billing himself

1087
00:45:53.660 --> 00:45:58.410
as the "Iron Cowboy", Lawrence aims to conquer 100

1088
00:45:58.410 --> 00:46:00.940
full distance triathlons in 100 days.

1089
00:46:00.940 --> 00:46:01.773
And this art,

1090
00:46:01.773 --> 00:46:05.093
which is kind of like a little bit of a backhanded,

1091
00:46:05.980 --> 00:46:08.883
not so nice way of introducing him,

1092
00:46:09.990 --> 00:46:13.280
this article proceeds to Chronicle

1093
00:46:13.280 --> 00:46:14.990
what he's attempting to do,

1094
00:46:14.990 --> 00:46:19.800
but it does it in a very kind of condescending way

1095
00:46:19.800 --> 00:46:21.770
and chooses to focus on things

1096
00:46:21.770 --> 00:46:24.240
that I think are not the point.

1097
00:46:24.240 --> 00:46:26.010
There's no mention of the community

1098
00:46:26.010 --> 00:46:27.720
and all these people that have come out,

1099
00:46:27.720 --> 00:46:30.240
this journalist didn't show up on the debt,

1100
00:46:30.240 --> 00:46:31.610
for any aspect of this,

1101
00:46:31.610 --> 00:46:33.410
to be boots on the ground who experienced

1102
00:46:33.410 --> 00:46:34.680
what was happening

1103
00:46:34.680 --> 00:46:39.160
and focused on things like, oh he takes an IV at night,

1104
00:46:39.160 --> 00:46:40.755
which is basically...

1105
00:46:40.755 --> 00:46:41.950
A couple of times a week.

1106
00:46:41.950 --> 00:46:43.540
To help himself recover,

1107
00:46:43.540 --> 00:46:46.100
which James has been extremely transparent about.

1108
00:46:46.100 --> 00:46:48.270
Basically tells you what he's doing and shows you

1109
00:46:48.270 --> 00:46:50.450
and says what's in the Iv.

1110
00:46:50.450 --> 00:46:52.310
And it's essentially the same thing

1111
00:46:52.310 --> 00:46:54.180
that you would get if you completed an Ironman

1112
00:46:54.180 --> 00:46:56.300
and went into the tent afterwards,

1113
00:46:56.300 --> 00:46:59.320
which is what a lot of people do at those races.

1114
00:46:59.320 --> 00:47:01.160
And then a bunch of other stuff

1115
00:47:01.160 --> 00:47:04.833
that just really is a distraction from,

1116
00:47:05.840 --> 00:47:10.380
what he was attempting to do without a lot of recognition

1117
00:47:10.380 --> 00:47:13.703
around just how extraordinarily difficult this is,

1118
00:47:15.280 --> 00:47:20.280
the kind of groundbreaking,

1119
00:47:20.590 --> 00:47:23.580
legendary aspect of doing something

1120
00:47:23.580 --> 00:47:25.883
that nobody had ever done before.

1121
00:47:26.730 --> 00:47:31.730
And I just thought it was lazy and uncool

1122
00:47:31.750 --> 00:47:35.263
I was like, why are you thought it was a hit piece?

1123
00:47:36.243 --> 00:47:37.843
And why even write this article?

1124
00:47:38.680 --> 00:47:39.830
I didn't understand it.

1125
00:47:40.930 --> 00:47:41.770
I can't speak for that reporter,

1126
00:47:41.770 --> 00:47:43.670
but most likely he would have loved to come out

1127
00:47:43.670 --> 00:47:46.320
and he probably just didn't get approved to come out.

1128
00:47:47.208 --> 00:47:49.160
And that's just a guest from me,

1129
00:47:49.160 --> 00:47:51.361
a guy sitting in a room, I have no idea

1130
00:47:51.361 --> 00:47:52.300
I have no connection to this reporter

1131
00:47:52.300 --> 00:47:53.600
or to the Washington post.

1132
00:47:54.713 --> 00:47:58.560
It focuses on criticism and controversy

1133
00:47:58.560 --> 00:48:00.790
with respect to his charity of choice.

1134
00:48:00.790 --> 00:48:04.980
And also some grumblings within the triathlon community

1135
00:48:04.980 --> 00:48:06.290
there was a bit of a controversy

1136
00:48:06.290 --> 00:48:08.290
when he did the 50, 50, 50,

1137
00:48:08.290 --> 00:48:10.480
because of weather conditions and logistics.

1138
00:48:10.480 --> 00:48:12.850
He was forced to do I don't know how,

1139
00:48:12.850 --> 00:48:15.610
like a marathon or two on an elliptical,

1140
00:48:15.610 --> 00:48:18.510
which was not his preference, which made people think,

1141
00:48:18.510 --> 00:48:20.520
well, he didn't really do this.

1142
00:48:20.520 --> 00:48:21.540
I think there was a couple of things

1143
00:48:21.540 --> 00:48:23.530
one was like, he did everything indoors

1144
00:48:23.530 --> 00:48:24.879
on a bad weather day.

1145
00:48:24.879 --> 00:48:25.712
And then the other thing,

1146
00:48:25.712 --> 00:48:26.810
he had an injury and he said,

1147
00:48:26.810 --> 00:48:28.520
and I think he did the marathon in elliptical

1148
00:48:28.520 --> 00:48:30.900
because as long as he's endorsed might not do that

1149
00:48:30.900 --> 00:48:33.460
witch or something like that, that's okay.

1150
00:48:33.460 --> 00:48:36.630
It gave people a reason to take them down a notch

1151
00:48:36.630 --> 00:48:38.980
and there's a snarkiness to all of this.

1152
00:48:38.980 --> 00:48:41.051
And I think one of them talks about why

1153
00:48:41.051 --> 00:48:42.220
(overlapping conversation)

1154
00:48:42.220 --> 00:48:43.790
Like what does why think of him doing these IVs?

1155
00:48:43.790 --> 00:48:45.760
And does this really count as a record?

1156
00:48:45.760 --> 00:48:47.090
Is this really a record at all?

1157
00:48:47.090 --> 00:48:49.730
The fact that the discussion is around whether

1158
00:48:49.730 --> 00:48:51.640
or not this is a record, like who cares?

1159
00:48:51.640 --> 00:48:52.700
I don't care if it's a record

1160
00:48:52.700 --> 00:48:54.840
who cares if it ends up in the Guinness book of world,

1161
00:48:54.840 --> 00:48:56.250
it's like, that's not the point.

1162
00:48:56.250 --> 00:48:58.170
The point is this guy went out and did something

1163
00:48:58.170 --> 00:49:01.240
unbelievably hard he did it with his friends.

1164
00:49:01.240 --> 00:49:04.180
He did it with whatever support that he could muster

1165
00:49:04.180 --> 00:49:07.160
and he impacted thousands if not hundreds of thousands

1166
00:49:07.160 --> 00:49:09.790
of people around the world who are now rethinking

1167
00:49:09.790 --> 00:49:13.020
their own perception of personal capability.

1168
00:49:13.020 --> 00:49:16.100
And the fact that this article didn't acknowledge

1169
00:49:16.100 --> 00:49:20.020
any aspect of that, I think is irresponsible.

1170
00:49:20.020 --> 00:49:22.840
And it bummed me out that this article even existed,

1171
00:49:22.840 --> 00:49:26.290
to me it's really a story that should be

1172
00:49:26.290 --> 00:49:31.290
all about basically what the thing is called conquering,

1173
00:49:32.765 --> 00:49:34.837
impossible and getting this impossible thing

1174
00:49:34.837 --> 00:49:36.930
and the impact that it's had on other people.

1175
00:49:36.930 --> 00:49:38.463
And you see other athletes,

1176
00:49:39.720 --> 00:49:42.400
it's very telling in who's flocked

1177
00:49:42.400 --> 00:49:44.530
to kind of be a part of this thing.

1178
00:49:44.530 --> 00:49:47.960
And people from all backgrounds all over the country,

1179
00:49:47.960 --> 00:49:50.360
he's getting messages from all over the world.

1180
00:49:50.360 --> 00:49:53.020
Other athletes are super impressed.

1181
00:49:53.020 --> 00:49:54.010
That was the big thing.

1182
00:49:54.010 --> 00:49:56.180
Well, like Tommy Rivers came out,

1183
00:49:56.180 --> 00:50:01.150
who's recovering from cancer is still in his struggle

1184
00:50:01.150 --> 00:50:04.593
and got through six miles with James, which was huge.

1185
00:50:06.030 --> 00:50:07.640
But the other thing is that

1186
00:50:08.910 --> 00:50:10.640
because there was this controversy

1187
00:50:10.640 --> 00:50:14.210
with the 50, 50, 50 with the elliptical and whatnot,

1188
00:50:14.210 --> 00:50:18.210
he really wanted to, quiet all of that and put it to bed.

1189
00:50:18.210 --> 00:50:21.000
So that's one reason I think that he decided

1190
00:50:21.000 --> 00:50:23.570
to do a hundred and then do 101.

1191
00:50:23.570 --> 00:50:25.040
And along the way,

1192
00:50:25.040 --> 00:50:28.020
if you go to places like Slow-twitch which is notorious

1193
00:50:28.020 --> 00:50:32.270
for a cantankerous forum section

1194
00:50:32.270 --> 00:50:34.563
where people like to take people down a peg,

1195
00:50:36.210 --> 00:50:38.520
he basically turned the tide there

1196
00:50:38.520 --> 00:50:41.560
and now has essentially unanimous support

1197
00:50:41.560 --> 00:50:45.030
from the endurance and multi-sport community at large.

1198
00:50:45.030 --> 00:50:46.560
It's funny is that one thing he said

1199
00:50:46.560 --> 00:50:49.330
that was disappointing and the whole team was saying

1200
00:50:49.330 --> 00:50:51.410
is that the local triathlon community

1201
00:50:51.410 --> 00:50:53.400
did not turn out for him.

1202
00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:57.540
And they never really understood why during the 50,

1203
00:50:57.540 --> 00:50:59.410
he was getting a lot of support until this,

1204
00:50:59.410 --> 00:51:00.911
that elliptical thing happened.

1205
00:51:00.911 --> 00:51:02.010
And then I don't know what happened.

1206
00:51:02.010 --> 00:51:04.610
It fell apart, but in the 100,

1207
00:51:04.610 --> 00:51:05.890
they weren't showing up,

1208
00:51:05.890 --> 00:51:07.170
they weren't showing up to the swims

1209
00:51:07.170 --> 00:51:08.150
they weren't showing up to the bikes,

1210
00:51:08.150 --> 00:51:09.863
they weren't showing up to the runs.

1211
00:51:11.298 --> 00:51:12.131
The people that really showed up

1212
00:51:12.131 --> 00:51:14.870
were the cyclists in Lindon and around...

1213
00:51:15.851 --> 00:51:17.504
A lot of cyclists in that area.

1214
00:51:17.504 --> 00:51:19.400
Because they were doing something of a criterion.

1215
00:51:19.400 --> 00:51:22.040
In the middle of pacing, like a 14 mile loop,

1216
00:51:22.040 --> 00:51:23.650
they would do it like three or four times

1217
00:51:23.650 --> 00:51:25.790
they'd ride there and then they would do

1218
00:51:25.790 --> 00:51:27.620
they'd do the loop and then they'd ride back.

1219
00:51:27.620 --> 00:51:31.820
And so they would have like the leaders,

1220
00:51:31.820 --> 00:51:34.180
they would be in the Peloton kind of like you said,

1221
00:51:34.180 --> 00:51:35.560
in the cut, like the end,

1222
00:51:35.560 --> 00:51:37.710
this Arrowhead of riders would take turns

1223
00:51:37.710 --> 00:51:39.640
and they'd switch off and they'd go hard

1224
00:51:39.640 --> 00:51:42.400
and lead the Park and break wind.

1225
00:51:42.400 --> 00:51:45.130
And so the cyclists really were heroes

1226
00:51:45.130 --> 00:51:46.250
and then the everyday people

1227
00:51:46.250 --> 00:51:48.800
who turned up were heroes.

1228
00:51:48.800 --> 00:51:52.550
It is weird that the triathletes couldn't show up for him.

1229
00:51:52.550 --> 00:51:54.270
Yeah, they thought it was weird, but you know...

1230
00:51:54.270 --> 00:51:56.280
It's a weird cultural thing.

1231
00:51:56.280 --> 00:51:58.963
And it's weird and I understand like,

1232
00:52:01.290 --> 00:52:04.500
for whatever it is, when you see a story

1233
00:52:04.500 --> 00:52:09.500
that's duplicitous or has several aspects to it,

1234
00:52:09.670 --> 00:52:11.120
there's something about that, that's good.

1235
00:52:11.120 --> 00:52:12.610
But at the same time, yes, you could

1236
00:52:12.610 --> 00:52:13.720
there's this version of story

1237
00:52:13.720 --> 00:52:15.430
where a lot of people told the story

1238
00:52:15.430 --> 00:52:16.760
without getting into the controversy.

1239
00:52:16.760 --> 00:52:18.010
They just wanted to tell the story

1240
00:52:18.010 --> 00:52:20.380
of this guy doing this hard thing.

1241
00:52:20.380 --> 00:52:25.380
And some editors like the multi-pronged approach,

1242
00:52:25.750 --> 00:52:27.250
because it's a more nuanced story.

1243
00:52:27.250 --> 00:52:28.730
And it's a little bit more,

1244
00:52:28.730 --> 00:52:30.123
just something to chew on.

1245
00:52:31.510 --> 00:52:33.000
Personally I was just glad to be there

1246
00:52:33.000 --> 00:52:34.510
and witness it that last day,

1247
00:52:34.510 --> 00:52:39.200
that finish was remarkable to get up every day with him

1248
00:52:39.200 --> 00:52:41.770
and even for me, just to get up every day.

1249
00:52:41.770 --> 00:52:44.660
The pool was hard I mean, at 5:00 AM

1250
00:52:44.660 --> 00:52:47.050
and he's getting five hours of sleep and he was like,

1251
00:52:47.050 --> 00:52:48.810
the stuff that didn't get into my stories,

1252
00:52:48.810 --> 00:52:51.930
his sleep was not like you'd expect him just to collapse

1253
00:52:51.930 --> 00:52:54.320
and like sleep hard, like a rock for five hours.

1254
00:52:54.320 --> 00:52:57.053
He said he was having night terrors waking up screaming.

1255
00:52:57.053 --> 00:52:58.060
Yeah, he told me about that,

1256
00:52:58.060 --> 00:53:02.550
night terrors, sweating profusely, like his sleep score.

1257
00:53:02.550 --> 00:53:04.620
He had this Bio-Tracker thing

1258
00:53:04.620 --> 00:53:07.390
and he was getting terrible sleep scores.

1259
00:53:07.390 --> 00:53:10.170
So he would go home at the end of the day,

1260
00:53:10.170 --> 00:53:12.210
get on the massage table,

1261
00:53:12.210 --> 00:53:14.510
get worked on fall asleep on the massage table,

1262
00:53:14.510 --> 00:53:19.030
move to the couch, get the NormaTec boots on

1263
00:53:19.030 --> 00:53:20.430
and essentially fall asleep.

1264
00:53:20.430 --> 00:53:21.870
But he never slept deeply,

1265
00:53:21.870 --> 00:53:23.250
he would have crazy dreams,

1266
00:53:23.250 --> 00:53:26.390
he was sleepwalking somewhat night terrors.

1267
00:53:26.390 --> 00:53:29.280
I never had night terrors wacky,

1268
00:53:29.280 --> 00:53:30.560
then on top of the whole thing,

1269
00:53:30.560 --> 00:53:32.770
I wanna get into kind of where he's at now,

1270
00:53:32.770 --> 00:53:34.120
physically and emotionally,

1271
00:53:35.360 --> 00:53:37.680
he was telling me on day 91,

1272
00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:40.070
that he could that for a long time,

1273
00:53:40.070 --> 00:53:45.070
he hasn't been able to feel anything in his two of his toes

1274
00:53:45.360 --> 00:53:47.340
on his left foot, not the big toe,

1275
00:53:47.340 --> 00:53:49.670
but the two next to the big toe.

1276
00:53:49.670 --> 00:53:52.370
And he said, I'm probably gonna have to,

1277
00:53:52.370 --> 00:53:53.260
it's a nerve thing.

1278
00:53:53.260 --> 00:53:54.690
It probably has to do with his back

1279
00:53:54.690 --> 00:53:56.820
and his hip or something like that.

1280
00:53:56.820 --> 00:53:58.470
But he has no feeling in them

1281
00:53:58.470 --> 00:54:01.840
and they might have to get removed

1282
00:54:01.840 --> 00:54:03.403
and he was okay with that.

1283
00:54:03.403 --> 00:54:04.236
(chuckles)

1284
00:54:04.236 --> 00:54:05.430
It's his idea I think.

1285
00:54:05.430 --> 00:54:07.413
He's like, let's just get rid of them.

1286
00:54:09.406 --> 00:54:11.850
So the links to which this guy has gone.

1287
00:54:11.850 --> 00:54:14.500
The extent to please do not be confused

1288
00:54:14.500 --> 00:54:17.440
like this guy has taken his body to the brain.

1289
00:54:17.440 --> 00:54:19.070
And if you've been following him in the days

1290
00:54:19.070 --> 00:54:21.670
that have elapsed, since he's completed this,

1291
00:54:21.670 --> 00:54:23.880
you see somebody who's struggling right now.

1292
00:54:23.880 --> 00:54:26.090
He immediately came down to LA

