3361
02:27:12.627 --> 02:27:13.940
And I was like, oh, you gotta be kidding me.

3362
02:27:13.940 --> 02:27:16.533
This is this unbelievable full circle moment.

3363
02:27:17.680 --> 02:27:19.900
And he came out,

3364
02:27:19.900 --> 02:27:22.210
I don't think he remembered this interaction by the way,

3365
02:27:22.210 --> 02:27:25.023
from 25 years prior, I was just some schmuck kid,

3366
02:27:26.420 --> 02:27:30.410
but I ran with them along the river.

3367
02:27:30.410 --> 02:27:32.560
And as we were going past towards one of the most scenic

3368
02:27:32.560 --> 02:27:35.633
areas of our entire city, he says to me,

3369
02:27:35.633 --> 02:27:37.690
I think I could live out here.

3370
02:27:37.690 --> 02:27:41.953
And maybe I'd like to start a youth running program to help,

3371
02:27:43.370 --> 02:27:45.940
some of these youth that might otherwise go down

3372
02:27:45.940 --> 02:27:47.200
the wrong route.

3373
02:27:47.200 --> 02:27:50.270
And I was like, oh my God, yes, we're gonna set this up

3374
02:27:50.270 --> 02:27:53.100
we recruited him, got him out here

3375
02:27:53.100 --> 02:27:57.210
and he's now running a whole program for largely Somali,

3376
02:27:57.210 --> 02:27:59.753
some not youth right around running.

3377
02:28:00.980 --> 02:28:01.813
Pretty cool.

3378
02:28:01.813 --> 02:28:02.823
Yeah, that's very cool.

3379
02:28:03.810 --> 02:28:08.810
I was speaking to Anthony Taylor earlier

3380
02:28:09.000 --> 02:28:10.163
who's very much,

3381
02:28:11.020 --> 02:28:16.020
in that world of trying to provide access to outdoor spaces

3382
02:28:16.270 --> 02:28:19.137
and outdoor activities to that community.

3383
02:28:19.137 --> 02:28:20.700
And it's super inspiring,

3384
02:28:20.700 --> 02:28:23.550
like work and there's so much work to be done there,

3385
02:28:23.550 --> 02:28:28.550
but perhaps the most kind of gratifying thing

3386
02:28:28.850 --> 02:28:30.250
that you could do it's cool.

3387
02:28:31.140 --> 02:28:33.050
So do you go out and run with them now?

3388
02:28:33.050 --> 02:28:35.477
Every now and again yeah we get in a run.

3389
02:28:39.060 --> 02:28:42.900
He's just such a jolly happy person

3390
02:28:42.900 --> 02:28:44.540
he's learning to cross country ski now,

3391
02:28:44.540 --> 02:28:46.093
which I am also,

3392
02:28:47.080 --> 02:28:50.040
I did not get out once this last winter,

3393
02:28:50.040 --> 02:28:52.180
but in general I try to get out the door.

3394
02:28:52.180 --> 02:28:53.013
I've never done that,

3395
02:28:53.013 --> 02:28:56.940
but it feels like a natural shift for anybody.

3396
02:28:56.940 --> 02:28:58.625
Who's an endurance runner.

3397
02:28:58.625 --> 02:29:00.275
It's not.
It's not?

3398
02:29:00.275 --> 02:29:01.108
It wasn't for me.

3399
02:29:01.108 --> 02:29:03.390
I know that it's really hard and it just kicks your ass.

3400
02:29:03.390 --> 02:29:05.130
Well, I don't, I never got my

3401
02:29:08.828 --> 02:29:10.000
it's a rhythm that you got to get into

3402
02:29:10.000 --> 02:29:11.730
and it's a whole motion,

3403
02:29:11.730 --> 02:29:13.270
especially if you're doing skate ski,

3404
02:29:13.270 --> 02:29:14.890
which is what I think is the,

3405
02:29:14.890 --> 02:29:16.620
that's the coolest most beautiful motion.

3406
02:29:16.620 --> 02:29:18.823
I mean, that's the one where you're going like this.

3407
02:29:19.707 --> 02:29:21.900
And I think for me,

3408
02:29:21.900 --> 02:29:26.440
I'm so used to the motion of the back kick of running

3409
02:29:26.440 --> 02:29:28.960
that the skate ski motion, just, I,

3410
02:29:28.960 --> 02:29:30.900
it just has taken me a while to learn,

3411
02:29:30.900 --> 02:29:33.550
not to mention I did not grow up skiing.

3412
02:29:33.550 --> 02:29:35.870
I didn't grow up ice skating, any of that.

3413
02:29:35.870 --> 02:29:40.870
And so this whole concept of you are in a relatively,

3414
02:29:41.310 --> 02:29:44.600
still position while the ground is moving under you.

3415
02:29:44.600 --> 02:29:45.433
You know what I mean?

3416
02:29:45.433 --> 02:29:47.300
You're sliding, that's not something

3417
02:29:47.300 --> 02:29:49.400
that I've really been comfortable with it.

3418
02:29:50.651 --> 02:29:53.080
There's a fluidity to it,

3419
02:29:53.080 --> 02:29:55.860
but your parents were both professional dancers.

3420
02:29:55.860 --> 02:29:59.260
So I feel like, yeah, you should be able to figure this out,

3421
02:29:59.260 --> 02:30:00.300
Figure It out, who knows?

3422
02:30:00.300 --> 02:30:01.860
Maybe, yeah.

3423
02:30:01.860 --> 02:30:04.880
What was that like two professional dancers?

3424
02:30:04.880 --> 02:30:06.580
I mean, that's a very interesting.

3425
02:30:08.930 --> 02:30:10.840
My parents met in New York City,

3426
02:30:10.840 --> 02:30:13.010
the dance for the Lubovitch Company in New York City

3427
02:30:13.010 --> 02:30:15.630
and then the Netherlands dance theater and Holland.

3428
02:30:15.630 --> 02:30:17.500
And they're pretty big time

3429
02:30:17.500 --> 02:30:21.040
my father was on the cover of like dancers magazine

3430
02:30:21.920 --> 02:30:26.920
and he hurt his back while he was in Belgium

3431
02:30:27.720 --> 02:30:30.180
and a chiropractor, fixed them up.

3432
02:30:30.180 --> 02:30:32.180
And he was kind of towards

3433
02:30:32.180 --> 02:30:33.500
the end of his dance career anyway.

3434
02:30:33.500 --> 02:30:36.010
So he decided to become a chiropractor,

3435
02:30:36.010 --> 02:30:37.340
moved back to the states

3436
02:30:38.440 --> 02:30:39.810
